    "text": "Businesses use accounting packages to record sales, purchases, invoices and ledgers, and payroll systems to calculate each worker's gross pay, deductions such as PAYE (Pay As You Earn) and NSSF (National Social Security Fund), and net pay, then print payslips. Banks use ICT (Information and Communication Technology) everywhere: automated teller machines (ATMs) let customers withdraw cash and check balances at any time using a card and PIN (Personal Identification Number); cheque clearing uses magnetic ink character recognition (MICR) to read the cheque number, bank code and account number printed in magnetic ink quickly and accurately (do not confuse it with OMR, optical mark recognition, which reads pencil marks on forms such as multiple-choice answer sheets); and internet and mobile banking let customers transfer money and pay bills without visiting a branch. M-Pesa is a form of electronic funds transfer (EFT): money moves from one account to another electronically, with no cash or cheque changing hands."
